{"mem_mq6vxslc_c85af89467fd":{"concepts":[],"content":"PinedIn v0.3.1 — A Tauri v2 desktop app built with React 18, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, framer-motion, and Zustand. It is a pinboard-style task manager with floating cards, reminders, workspaces, and a system tray. The app uses Tauri's window API for draggable, closable card windows and SQL plugin for persistence.","createdAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:52.700Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mq6vxslc_c85af89467fd","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"PinedIn v0.3.1 — A Tauri v2 desktop app built with React 18, TypeScript, Tailwin","type":"fact","updatedAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:52.700Z","version":1},"mem_mq6vxspu_3cc2f79e7fef":{"concepts":[],"content":"Recent commit history of PinedIn:\n1e7847e fix(updater): switch to v1Compatible artifacts, fix latest.json generation\n7d4a657 release: v0.3.1\ndb86c2e fix(ci): upload .exe instead of .msi for Windows NSIS installer\n213f062 fix(ui): move Workspaces button to Tasks header, add workspace detail view\n2e9d33c fix(build): conditionally compile transparent() to fix macOS build\nd1b7d32 fix(changelog): correct section ordering to reverse chronological\n72b4254 release: bump version to v0.3.0\n1bfaae3 fix: prevent permanent drag freeze on task cards, make close handler survive hide() failure\n8667e0d feat(workspaces): redesign as full page view with card grid layout\nf246be8 fix(ci): generate latest.json for public repo, fix repo ref, upload update archives\n075414a fix: update updater public key with newly generated signing keypair\nbe47dcf fix(updater): point endpoint to public PinedIn-Releases repo\nc2d8749 feat(ci): add macOS/Linux matrix build, upload to public releases repo\n34d7835 feat(bundle): add dmg/appimage/deb targets, macOS min version, linux config\ndf53a56 fix(window): add Linux compositor detection for transparency fallback\ne1cee4c fix(tray): macOS left-click shows menu, exclude double-click handler\n808a94b fix(lib): wrap hide/show in cfg(windows), add platform-aware shortcut\n5925bad fix(main): guard windows_subsystem with target_os cfg\n125e446 ﻿fix(ui): pure black shiny text in light mode via dedicated CSS vars\na42ced1 ﻿fix(ui): import CSS variables in daily-digest context, fix hardcoded black bg\n1797713 ﻿fix(ui): replace TaskCard hardcoded white bar color with CSS variable\nbe9ea2f ﻿fix(ui): replace QuickAdd hardcoded error colors with CSS variables\n1146c6a ﻿fix(ui): replace ShinyText hardcoded colors with CSS variables for theme adaptation\ne638ec2 ﻿fix(ui): replace hardcoded logo colors with CSS variables for theme support\n11c1049 ﻿refactor(task-card): remove unused URGENCY_LABEL constant\n3357276 ﻿fix(ui): move settings gear next to PinedIn title text\n9a26b0b ﻿feat(ui): collapsible completed section with caret toggle + Clear All\na968341 ﻿fix(ui): remove extra undo button, use checkbox toggle for restore\n9fd3067 ﻿feat(ui): add undo for completed tasks with cross-window sync\n55dab8d ﻿feat(ui): move Settings button to titlebar as gear icon\n0567c56 ﻿fix(theme): clean up system media listener when switching away from system mode\n9caff7c ﻿fix(task-card): enable double-click expand, defer startDragging until after 6px move\n60ff69b ﻿fix(ui): add v-btn hover effect to Zen, Align, Pre-Schedule buttons\ne04e20b fix(task-card): detect click vs drag via pointer threshold\nd654efc Fix shake animation overriding card background in light mode\n61981ea Add system theme listener for OS-level dark mode changes\nc90ec5e Add cross-window theme sync: Rust emit + secondary window listeners\n37090b9 Convert QuickAdd.tsx and DailyDigest.tsx inline colors to CSS variables\n839d9af Convert TaskCard.tsx and task-card.css to CSS variable references\n37b00ce Convert PreScheduleModal, WorkspacePanel, UpdateBanner inline colors to CSS variables\n47b1718 Convert SettingsPanel.tsx inline colors to CSS variable references\nd7e509a Convert AddTaskModal.tsx inline colors to CSS variable references\n3ac662c Convert TaskList.tsx inline colors to CSS variable references\n4baba10 Convert App.tsx inline colors to CSS variable references\n562b350 Add light/dark CSS variables to index.css and task-card.css\ncd280ff feat(ui): add glow + scale hover effect to .v-btn and .v-action buttons\n1808836 fix(ui): strip archive zone remnants and dead interacting ref from TaskCard\na031164 chore: remove duplicate expandedRef.current assignment\n47331eb feat: remove Drag-to-Archive zone feature entirely\nba77bd4 fix(ui): rewrite TaskCard drag and click logic with clean window-level mouseup handler\nef2ef08 feat(ui): create WorkspacePanel dropdown component for profile management\n1ce1f24 feat(ui): add Zen Mode toggle, Align button, and WorkspacePanel to toolbar\n9e62610 feat(ui): add creation timestamp, drag-to-archive, and shake-to-align to TaskCard\n1a6f569 ﻿feat(core): add Zen Mode, Archive Zone, Snap-to-Grid, and Workspace Profiles backend\n93bd5eb chore(build): add archive-zone.html entry to Vite multi-page config\nd5d40ed feat(ui): add drag-to-archive drop zone component and entry point\n0481faf fix(core): reset started_at on task edit to restart progress timer\na5dbe79 fix(ui): remove delete confirmation dialog from task list\ne582381 fix(ui): tighten ShinyText gradient stops for brighter shine\n6c00a78 chore(icons): swap to rounded-checkbox fading-rows app icon\ndbafcdf feat(ui): add ShinyText to titlebar and task header\nec5dbae fix: timezone, double-close, type-safety, and v0.2.1 sync\nb143cb8 chore(icons): swap to fading-rows app icon\nd480551 release: bump version to v0.2.1\ndb6d612 Add image and logo to README\n4366186 Actual Tray fix\n7002432 Fixing the Tray\n1f688d2 fix(tray): make minimize-to-tray bulletproof and prep v0.2.0\ndfe4267 feat(pre-schedule): schedule a task to spawn at a future datetime\n60c7a3b fix(window): hide main window on close instead of exiting\n4697ae4 fix(task-card): clip time-limit progress bar to card's rounded corners\nca764b7 fix(release): grant workflow write permission to create releases\nc7e2857 fix(release): encode full .pub file as updater pubkey\n500bd5d feat(time-limit): live countdown progress bar on floating task cards\n06467ad fix(release): align updater pubkey and env var with Tauri CLI v2\ne90ef6c fix(tauri): correct plugin API usage for v2.10.1 / 2.3.1 / 2.3.2\nfa5df52 feat(daily-digest): show summary popup 2s after launch with 10s auto-dismiss\n9e1fd5b feat(updater): one-click update via GitHub Releases with in-app banner\naeb750f feat(quick-add): hardcode critical+due-today on hotkey submit\n4e7b453 feat(ui): add global hotkey quick-add popup component\n27cf380 feat(build): add quick-add.html as vite entry point\nb818e77 feat(tauri): add open_quick_add_window function and helpers\n4e7bcca feat(tauri): register Ctrl+Shift+Space global shortcut on startup\n2d251db feat(tauri): add global-shortcut plugin and permissions\nef9c501 feat(css): bump shared class font sizes by 1px for readability\n1f429cb feat(ui): bump SettingsPanel font sizes by 1px for readability\nc9f9cdd feat(ui): bump AddTaskModal font sizes by 1px for readability\n25f2f4c feat(ui): bump task list font sizes by 1px for readability\n5b2aea7 feat(ui): bump main app font sizes by 1px for readability\n1f50749 feat(css): add .dot live status indicator styles\n86503fc feat(ui): add live heartbeat dot to main app header\n6223737 feat(css): refresh floating card styles, add dot, bump contrast\ndb77091 refactor(ui): two-size card, heartbeat dot, contrast pass\n95f9c9b feat(tauri): bump floating card height to 120px\nca944a6 feat(updater): set real minisign pubkey and guard keys in gitignore\ndb735d2 Merge branch 'fix/audit-issues': full audit fix pass\n2fdd108 feat(ui): surface action errors in task list\nfa980be refactor(ui): use UrgencyBadge component in TaskCard\n998671c fix(ui): show human-readable dates on floating task cards\n5a193db refactor(db): make migrations explicit and include all columns in CREATE TABLE\n\nFull history available via 'git log'.","createdAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:52.858Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mq6vxspu_3cc2f79e7fef","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"Recent commit history of PinedIn:\n1e7847e fix(updater): switch to v1Compatible a","type":"fact","updatedAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:52.858Z","version":1},"mem_mq6vxsrw_d60310619b31":{"concepts":[],"content":"File: src/App.tsx\n\nimport { useState, useEffect, useRef } from \"react\";\nimport { getCurrentWindow } from \"@tauri-apps/api/window\";\nimport { listen } from \"@tauri-apps/api/event\";\nimport TaskList from \"@/components/TaskList\";\nimport AddTaskModal from \"@/components/AddTaskModal\";\nimport SettingsPanel from \"@/components/SettingsPanel\";\nimport PreScheduleModal from \"@/components/PreScheduleModal\";\nimport ShinyText from \"@/components/ui/ShinyText\";\nimport UpdateBanner from \"@/components/UpdateBanner\";\nimport WorkspacesView from \"@/components/WorkspacesView\";\nimport WorkspaceDetailView from \"@/components/WorkspaceDetailView\";\nimport { useReminders } from \"@/hooks/useReminders\";\nimport { useReminderStore } from \"@/store/reminderStore\";\nimport { getShakeInterval, setShakeInterval, setZenMode, snapAllCardsToGrid } from \"@/lib/tauriCommands\";\n\nconst SHAKE_OPTIONS = [10, 15, 30, 60, 120, 300];\n\nexport default function App() {\n  useReminders();\n\n  const tasks = useReminderStore((s) => s.tasks);\n  const fetchTasks = useReminderStore((s) => s.fetchTasks);\n  const isAddTaskOpen = useReminderStore((s) => s.isAddTaskOpen);\n  const setAddTaskOpen = useReminderStore((s) => s.setAddTaskOpen);\n  const isSettingsOpen = useReminderStore((s) => s.isSettingsOpen);\n  const setSettingsOpen = useReminderStore((s) => s.setSettingsOpen);\n  const isPreScheduleOpen = useReminderStore((s) => s.isPreScheduleOpen);\n  const setPreScheduleOpen = useReminderStore((s) => s.setPreScheduleOpen);\n  const editingTask = useReminderStore((s) => s.editingTask);\n  const setEditingTask = useReminderStore((s) => s.setEditingTask);\n  const isPaused = useReminderStore((s) => s.isPaused);\n  const togglePaused = useReminderStore((s) => s.togglePaused);\n\n  type AppView =\n    | { type: \"tasks\" }\n    | { type: \"workspaces\" }\n    | { type: \"workspace-detail\"; workspaceId: number; workspaceName: string };\n\n  const [view, setView] = useState<AppView>({ type: \"tasks\" });\n\n  // Listen for task edit triggers from floating cards\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const unlisten = listen<number>(\"open_edit_task\", (event) => {\n      const taskId = event.payload;\n      const task = tasks.find((t) => t.id === taskId);\n      if (task) {\n        setEditingTask(task);\n      }\n    });\n    return () => {\n      unlisten.then((f) => f());\n    };\n  }, [tasks, setEditingTask]);\n\n  // Refresh task list when backend emits tasks-updated\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const unlisten = listen(\"tasks-updated\", () => {\n      fetchTasks();\n    });\n    return () => {\n      unlisten.then((f) => f());\n    };\n  }, [fetchTasks]);\n\n  // Close any open modal on Escape key\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const handleKeyDown = (e: KeyboardEvent) => {\n      if (e.key !== \"Escape\") return;\n      if (isAddTaskOpen) {\n        setAddTaskOpen(false);\n        setEditingTask(null);\n      }\n      if (isSettingsOpen) {\n        setSettingsOpen(false);\n      }\n      if (isPreScheduleOpen) {\n        setPreScheduleOpen(false);\n      }\n    };\n    window.addEventListener(\"keydown\", handleKeyDown);\n    return () => window.removeEventListener(\"keydown\", handleKeyDown);\n  }, [\n    isAddTaskOpen,\n    isSettingsOpen,\n    isPreScheduleOpen,\n    setAddTaskOpen,\n    setSettingsOpen,\n    setPreScheduleOpen,\n    setEditingTask,\n  ]);\n\n  const [zenMode, setZenModeState] = useState(false);\n\n  async function toggleZenMode() {\n    const next = !zenMode;\n    setZenModeState(next);\n    await setZenMode(next).catch(() => {});\n  }\n\n  const [searchQuery, setSearchQuery] = useState(\"\");\n  const incompleteCount = tasks.filter((t) => !t.completed).length;\n  const isAnyModalOpen = isAddTaskOpen || isSettingsOpen || isPreScheduleOpen;\n\n  const [shakeInterval, setShakeIntervalLocal] = useState<number>(30);\n  useEffect(() => {\n    getShakeInterval()\n      .then((s) => setShakeIntervalLocal(s))\n      .catch(() => {});\n  }, []);\n\n  const handleShakeChange = (value: number) => {\n    setShakeIntervalLocal(value);\n    setShakeInterval(value).catch(() => {});\n  };\n\n  const liveDotRef = useRef<HTMLSpanElement>","createdAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:52.934Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mq6vxsrw_d60310619b31","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"File: src/App.tsx\n\nimport { useState, useEffect, useRef } from \"react\";\nimport {","type":"fact","updatedAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:52.934Z","version":1},"mem_mq6vxssq_4ab4bf674b95":{"concepts":[],"content":"File: src-tauri/src/lib.rs\n\npub mod commands;\r\npub mod db;\r\npub mod notifications;\r\npub mod scheduler;\r\npub mod tray;\r\npub mod window;\r\n\r\nuse db::DbHandle;\r\nuse std::sync::atomic::{AtomicBool, Ordering};\r\nuse std::sync::Arc;\r\nuse tauri::{Emitter, Manager};\r\nuse tauri_plugin_autostart::MacosLauncher;\r\nuse tauri_plugin_global_shortcut::{Code, GlobalShortcutExt, Modifiers, Shortcut};\r\nuse tauri_plugin_notification::NotificationExt;\r\nuse tauri_plugin_window_state::StateFlags;\r\n\r\n/// Shared flag flipped to `true` when the user explicitly chooses to quit\r\n/// (via the tray menu). The main window's close handler checks this so\r\n/// that the *next* close actually kills the process instead of\r\n/// minimizing to tray. This is what lets the user fully close the app\r\n/// after it's been living in the tray.\r\n#[derive(Default)]\r\npub struct QuitFlag(pub Arc<AtomicBool>);\r\n\r\n#[cfg_attr(mobile, tauri::mobile_entry_point)]\r\npub fn run() {\r\n    tauri::Builder::default()\r\n        .plugin(\r\n            tauri_plugin_window_state::Builder::default()\r\n                // Deny-list the main window: we own its close behaviour\r\n                // (minimize-to-tray), and the plugin's own close handler\r\n                // would otherwise race with ours and destroy the window.\r\n                .with_denylist(&[\"main\"])\r\n                .build(),\r\n        )\r\n        .plugin(tauri_plugin_notification::init())\r\n        .plugin(tauri_plugin_autostart::init(\r\n            MacosLauncher::LaunchAgent,\r\n            Some(vec![]),\r\n        ))\r\n        .plugin(tauri_plugin_updater::Builder::new().build())\r\n        .plugin(tauri_plugin_process::init())\r\n        .plugin(tauri_plugin_global_shortcut::Builder::new().build())\r\n        .setup(|app| {\r\n            // Register the quit flag in app state so the tray menu and\r\n            // the close handler can both reach it.\r\n            let quit_flag = QuitFlag::default();\r\n            app.manage(quit_flag);\r\n\r\n            let app_data_dir = app\r\n                .path()\r\n                .app_data_dir()\r\n                .expect(\"Failed to get app data directory\");\r\n\r\n            let db_handle =\r\n                Arc::new(DbHandle::new(app_data_dir).expect(\"Failed to initialize database\"));\r\n\r\n            app.manage(db_handle.clone());\r\n\r\n            let main_window = app.get_webview_window(\"main\").unwrap();\r\n            let main_window_clone = main_window.clone();\r\n\r\n            // Register the close-to-tray handler FIRST, before any\r\n            // hide()/show() dance. Tauri delivers WindowEvent to handlers\r\n            // attached to the window; re-creating the window visually\r\n            // (hide+show) is safe but doing it before the handler is\r\n            // bound opens a brief window where a real close could slip\r\n            // through. Bind first, decorate second.\r\n            let quit_flag_handle = app.state::<QuitFlag>().0.clone();\r\n            main_window.on_window_event(move |event| {\r\n                if let tauri::WindowEvent::CloseRequested { api, .. } = event {\r\n                    // If the user picked \"Quit PinedIn\" from the tray,\r\n                    // the flag is set — let the close go through so the\r\n                    // process actually exits.\r\n                    if quit_flag_handle.load(Ordering::SeqCst) {\r\n                        return;\r\n                    }\r\n                    api.prevent_close();\r\n                    // Only hide if the window is currently visible.\r\n                    // If hide() fails (e.g. window is already destroyed),\r\n                    // we don't want the user stuck in a prevent-close loop.\r\n                    if main_window_clone.is_visible().unwrap_or(false) {\r\n                        if main_window_clone.hide().is_err() {\r\n                            // hide failed — window might be in a bad state.\r\n                            // Let the close go through as a last resort.\r\n                        }\r\n                    }\r\n                }\r\n            });\r\n\r\n            // Force remove nativ","createdAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:52.966Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mq6vxssq_4ab4bf674b95","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"File: src-tauri/src/lib.rs\n\npub mod commands;\r\npub mod db;\r\npub mod notification","type":"fact","updatedAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:52.966Z","version":1},"mem_mq6vxstv_022a6f452ad1":{"concepts":[],"content":"File: src-tauri/src/main.rs\n\n// Prevents additional console window on Windows in release\n#![cfg_attr(\n    all(not(debug_assertions), target_os = \"windows\"),\n    windows_subsystem = \"windows\"\n)]\n\nfn main() {\n    pinedin_lib::run();\n}","createdAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.005Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mq6vxstv_022a6f452ad1","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"File: src-tauri/src/main.rs\n\n// Prevents additional console window on Windows in","type":"fact","updatedAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.005Z","version":1},"mem_mq6vxsul_8d60dd70883d":{"concepts":[],"content":"File: src-tauri/src/tray.rs\n\nuse crate::QuitFlag;\nuse std::sync::atomic::Ordering;\nuse tauri::{\n    image::Image,\n    menu::{MenuBuilder, MenuItemBuilder},\n    tray::{MouseButton, MouseButtonState, TrayIconBuilder, TrayIconEvent},\n    Emitter, Manager,\n};\n\n/// Setup the system tray with menu items and event handlers.\n/// Clicking the tray icon toggles the main window's visibility so the\n/// app stays running in the background between sessions, exactly like\n/// Discord or Spotify. Only the explicit \"Quit PinedIn\" menu item\n/// actually kills the process; it flips the shared `QuitFlag` and then\n/// calls `app.exit(0)` so the main window's close-to-tray handler\n/// knows to let the next close event through to the OS.\npub fn setup_tray(app: &tauri::AppHandle) -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {\n    let show_app = MenuItemBuilder::with_id(\"show_app\", \"Show App\").build(app)?;\n    let quick_task = MenuItemBuilder::with_id(\"quick_task\", \"Add Quick Task\").build(app)?;\n    let quit = MenuItemBuilder::with_id(\"quit\", \"Quit PinedIn\").build(app)?;\n\n    let menu = MenuBuilder::new(app)\n        .item(&show_app)\n        .item(&quick_task)\n        .separator()\n        .item(&quit)\n        .build()?;\n\n    // On Windows the tray icon MUST have an icon set, otherwise it\n    // won't appear in the notification area at all. Fall back from\n    // the bundle's default window icon to a 1x1 transparent image so\n    // the build never fails on a missing-asset edge case.\n    let icon: Image<'_> = app\n        .default_window_icon()\n        .cloned()\n        .ok_or(\"missing default window icon for tray\")?;\n\n    // macOS convention: menu bar icons show menu on left-click.\n    // Windows/Linux: left-click toggles the app window instead.\n    #[cfg(target_os = \"macos\")]\n    let show_menu = true;\n    #[cfg(not(target_os = \"macos\"))]\n    let show_menu = false;\n\n    let tray = TrayIconBuilder::new()\n        .icon(icon)\n        .tooltip(\"PinedIn\")\n        .menu(&menu)\n        .show_menu_on_left_click(show_menu)\n        .on_menu_event(move |app_handle, event| match event.id().as_ref() {\n            \"show_app\" => {\n                if let Some(window) = app_handle.get_webview_window(\"main\") {\n                    let _ = window.show();\n                    let _ = window.unminimize();\n                    let _ = window.set_focus();\n                }\n            }\n            \"quick_task\" => {\n                let _ = app_handle.emit(\"open-quick-task\", ());\n                if let Some(window) = app_handle.get_webview_window(\"main\") {\n                    let _ = window.show();\n                    let _ = window.unminimize();\n                    let _ = window.set_focus();\n                }\n            }\n            \"quit\" => {\n                // Flip the shared quit flag so the main window's\n                // CloseRequested handler lets the next close go\n                // through to the OS, then ask Tauri to exit. This\n                // gives a clean shutdown (DB closes, plugins unload)\n                // instead of the abrupt std::process::exit(0).\n                let flag = app_handle.state::<QuitFlag>();\n                flag.0.store(true, Ordering::SeqCst);\n                app_handle.exit(0);\n            }\n            _ => {}\n        })\n        .on_tray_icon_event(|tray, event| {\n            // Left click and double click both toggle the main window:\n            // show+focus if hidden, hide if visible.\n            // Note: TrayIconEvent::DoubleClick does not fire reliably\n            // on macOS menu bar icons, so it's excluded on that platform.\n            let should_toggle = matches!(\n                event,\n                TrayIconEvent::Click {\n                    button: MouseButton::Left,\n                    button_state: MouseButtonState::Up,\n                    ..\n                }\n            ) || (cfg!(not(target_os = \"macos\"))\n                && matches!(event, TrayIconEvent::DoubleClick { .. }));\n            if should_toggle {\n                let app = tray.app_handle();\n   ","createdAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.029Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mq6vxsul_8d60dd70883d","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"File: src-tauri/src/tray.rs\n\nuse crate::QuitFlag;\nuse std::sync::atomic::Orderin","type":"fact","updatedAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.029Z","version":1},"mem_mq6vxsvn_e3afea3f2240":{"concepts":[],"content":"File: src-tauri/src/window.rs\n\nuse crate::commands::ZEN_MODE;\nuse crate::db::Task;\nuse std::sync::atomic::Ordering;\nuse tauri::{AppHandle, LogicalPosition, LogicalSize, Manager, WebviewUrl, WebviewWindowBuilder};\n\n/// Returns `true` if the platform supports transparent windows.\n/// On Linux, transparency requires a compositing window manager;\n/// Wayland and non-compositing X11 sessions fall back to opaque.\nfn supports_transparency() -> bool {\n    #[cfg(target_os = \"linux\")]\n    {\n        // Check for Wayland — transparency is unreliable there\n        if std::env::var(\"WAYLAND_DISPLAY\").is_ok()\n            || std::env::var(\"XDG_SESSION_TYPE\")\n                .map(|v| v == \"wayland\")\n                .unwrap_or(false)\n        {\n            return false;\n        }\n        // X11 without compositor: check for common compositor env vars\n        if std::env::var(\"XDG_SESSION_TYPE\")\n            .map(|v| v == \"x11\")\n            .unwrap_or(false)\n        {\n            // Assume compositor is present (most modern desktops).\n            // Users on bare X11 without a compositor get opaque windows,\n            // which is still functional.\n            return true;\n        }\n    }\n    // macOS and Windows support transparency natively\n    true\n}\n\nconst CARD_WIDTH: f64 = 280.0;\nconst CARD_HEIGHT: f64 = 120.0;\nconst TOP_MARGIN: f64 = 80.0;\nconst RIGHT_MARGIN: f64 = 24.0;\nconst CARD_GAP: f64 = 12.0;\n\nconst QUICK_ADD_WIDTH: f64 = 480.0;\nconst QUICK_ADD_HEIGHT: f64 = 64.0;\nconst QUICK_ADD_TOP_MARGIN: f64 = 120.0;\n\nfn monitor_size(app: &AppHandle) -> (f64, f64) {\n    if let Some(monitor) = app.primary_monitor().ok().flatten().or_else(|| {\n        app.available_monitors()\n            .ok()\n            .and_then(|m| m.into_iter().next())\n    }) {\n        let scale = monitor.scale_factor();\n        let size = monitor.size();\n        return (size.width as f64 / scale, size.height as f64 / scale);\n    }\n    (1920.0, 1080.0)\n}\n\n/// Horizontal center position for the quick-add popup, in logical pixels.\nfn get_center_x(app: &AppHandle) -> f64 {\n    let (screen_w, _) = monitor_size(app);\n    ((screen_w - QUICK_ADD_WIDTH) / 2.0).max(0.0)\n}\n\n/// Vertical top position for the quick-add popup. Sits in the upper\n/// third of the screen like Spotlight / Raycast, leaving the rest of\n/// the desktop visible below.\nfn get_top_y(_app: &AppHandle) -> f64 {\n    QUICK_ADD_TOP_MARGIN\n}\n\n/// Sum the height of all currently-open task card windows.\nfn stack_offset_y(app: &AppHandle) -> f64 {\n    let mut max_bottom = TOP_MARGIN;\n    let windows = app.webview_windows();\n    for (label, window) in windows.iter() {\n        if !label.starts_with(\"task_\") {\n            continue;\n        }\n        if let (Ok(pos), Ok(size)) = (window.outer_position(), window.outer_size()) {\n            let scale = window.scale_factor().unwrap_or(1.0);\n            let logical_y = pos.y as f64 / scale;\n            let logical_h = size.height as f64 / scale;\n            let bottom = logical_y + logical_h;\n            if bottom > max_bottom {\n                max_bottom = bottom;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    max_bottom\n}\n\n/// Create a small always-on-top window for a single task card.\n/// Windows are stacked vertically starting from the top-right of the\n/// primary monitor, beneath any cards that are already open.\npub fn open_task_card(app: &AppHandle, task: &Task, _index: usize) -> Result<(), String> {\n    let id = match task.id {\n        Some(id) => id,\n        None => return Err(\"Task has no ID\".into()),\n    };\n\n    let label = format!(\"task_{}\", id);\n\n    // Don't recreate if already exists\n    if app.get_webview_window(&label).is_some() {\n        return Ok(());\n    }\n\n    let (screen_w, _) = monitor_size(app);\n    let x = (screen_w - CARD_WIDTH - RIGHT_MARGIN).max(0.0);\n    let y = stack_offset_y(app) + CARD_GAP;\n\n    let builder = WebviewWindowBuilder::new(app, &label, WebviewUrl::App(\"task-card.html\".into()))\n        .inner_size(CARD_WIDTH, CARD_HEIGHT)\n        .resizable(false)\n        .decorations(false);\n\n    #[cfg","createdAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.068Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mq6vxsvn_e3afea3f2240","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"File: src-tauri/src/window.rs\n\nuse crate::commands::ZEN_MODE;\nuse crate::db::Tas","type":"fact","updatedAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.068Z","version":1},"mem_mq6vxswl_14663bfc431f":{"concepts":[],"content":"File: src-tauri/tauri.conf.json\n\n{\r\n  \"$schema\": \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tauri-apps/tauri/dev/crates/tauri-config-schema/schema.json\",\r\n  \"productName\": \"PinedIn\",\r\n  \"version\": \"0.3.1\",\r\n  \"identifier\": \"com.pinedin.desktop\",\r\n  \"build\": {\r\n    \"frontendDist\": \"../dist\",\r\n    \"devUrl\": \"http://localhost:1420\",\r\n    \"beforeDevCommand\": \"npm run dev\",\r\n    \"beforeBuildCommand\": \"npm run build\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"app\": {\r\n    \"windows\": [\r\n      {\r\n        \"label\": \"main\",\r\n        \"title\": \"PinedIn\",\r\n        \"width\": 900,\r\n        \"height\": 650,\r\n        \"resizable\": true,\r\n        \"closable\": true,\r\n        \"visible\": true,\r\n        \"decorations\": false,\r\n        \"transparent\": true,\r\n        \"shadow\": true,\r\n        \"fullscreen\": false,\r\n        \"center\": true,\r\n        \"minWidth\": 600,\r\n        \"minHeight\": 400\r\n      }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"security\": {\r\n      \"csp\": null\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"bundle\": {\r\n    \"active\": true,\r\n    \"targets\": [\"nsis\", \"dmg\", \"appimage\", \"deb\"],\r\n    \"icon\": [\r\n      \"icons/32x32.png\",\r\n      \"icons/128x128.png\",\r\n      \"icons/128x128@2x.png\",\r\n      \"icons/icon.icns\",\r\n      \"icons/icon.ico\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"resources\": [],\r\n    \"externalBin\": [],\r\n    \"copyright\": \"\",\r\n    \"category\": \"Productivity\",\r\n    \"shortDescription\": \"Floating task overlay for your desktop\",\r\n    \"longDescription\": \"PinedIn keeps your tasks floating on screen no matter what app you are using.\",\r\n    \"createUpdaterArtifacts\": \"v1Compatible\",\r\n    \"windows\": {\r\n      \"wix\": null,\r\n      \"nsis\": {\r\n        \"installMode\": \"perMachine\",\r\n        \"displayLanguageSelector\": false,\r\n        \"languages\": [\"English\"],\r\n        \"installerIcon\": \"icons/icon.ico\",\r\n        \"headerImage\": \"icons/installer-header.bmp\",\r\n        \"sidebarImage\": \"icons/installer-sidebar.bmp\"\r\n      }\r\n    },\r\n    \"macOS\": {\r\n      \"minimumSystemVersion\": \"12.0\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"linux\": {\r\n      \"deb\": {\r\n        \"depends\": []\r\n      },\r\n      \"appimage\": {\r\n        \"bundleMediaFramework\": true\r\n      }\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"plugins\": {\r\n    \"updater\": {\r\n      \"active\": true,\r\n      \"dialog\": false,\r\n      \"pubkey\": \"dW50cnVzdGVkIGNvbW1lbnQ6IG1pbmlzaWduIHB1YmxpYyBrZXk6IEZGRTA0NUFCQjBCMDJFRjQKUldUMExyQ3dxMFhnLzJ2VDcrT0d3TWtIYUdRb0tYcDRMMmFoN3hCTmlnWXV6T05mdXp0UXlOa0wK\",\r\n      \"endpoints\": [\r\n        \"https://github.com/Zarl-prog/PinedIn-Releases/releases/latest/download/latest.json\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"dangerousInsecureTransportProtocol\": false\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n}","createdAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.103Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mq6vxswl_14663bfc431f","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"File: src-tauri/tauri.conf.json\n\n{\r\n  \"$schema\": \"https://raw.githubusercontent.","type":"fact","updatedAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.103Z","version":1},"mem_mq6vxsxc_c61361b72162":{"concepts":[],"content":"File: src-tauri/Cargo.toml\n\n[package]\nname = \"pinedin\"\nversion = \"0.3.1\"\ndescription = \"PinedIn - Always-on-top focus reminder app\"\nauthors = [\"PinedIn\"]\nedition = \"2021\"\n\n[lib]\nname = \"pinedin_lib\"\ncrate-type = [\"staticlib\", \"cdylib\", \"rlib\"]\n\n[build-dependencies]\ntauri-build = { version = \"2\", features = [] }\n\n[dependencies]\ntauri = { version = \"2\", features = [\"tray-icon\"] }\ntauri-plugin-window-state = \"2\"\nserde = { version = \"1\", features = [\"derive\"] }\nserde_json = \"1\"\nchrono = { version = \"0.4\", features = [\"serde\"] }\nrusqlite = { version = \"0.31\", features = [\"bundled\"] }\ntauri-plugin-notification = \"2\"\ntauri-plugin-autostart = \"2\"\ntauri-plugin-updater = \"2\"\ntauri-plugin-process = \"2\"\ntauri-plugin-global-shortcut = \"2\"\n\n[profile.release]\nopt-level = 3\nlto = true\ncodegen-units = 1\nstrip = true\npanic = \"abort\"","createdAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.128Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mq6vxsxc_c61361b72162","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"File: src-tauri/Cargo.toml\n\n[package]\nname = \"pinedin\"\nversion = \"0.3.1\"\ndescrip","type":"fact","updatedAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.128Z","version":1},"mem_mq6vxsy3_a689d81b01bf":{"concepts":[],"content":"File: src/index.css\n\n@import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist+Mono:wght@400;500;600&display=swap');\n\n:root {\n  --bg-app: #ffffff;\n  --bg-card: #f5f5f5;\n  --bg-card-hover: #f0f0f0;\n  --bg-float: #ffffff;\n  --bg-float-hover: #fafafa;\n  --bg-input: #ffffff;\n  --bg-hover: #e8e8e8;\n  --bg-badge: #e8e8e8;\n  --bg-overlay: rgba(0,0,0,0.3);\n  --bg-toggle: #d0d0d0;\n  --bg-modal: #ffffff;\n  --bg-update: #f5f5f5;\n  --bg-menu: #ffffff;\n  --bg-menu-hover: #f0f0f0;\n  --bg-delete-hover: #ffe8e8;\n  --bg-dropdown: #ffffff;\n  --bg-scheduled: #f5f5f5;\n  --bg-date-icon: #999999;\n  --bg-tag: #e8e8e8;\n\n  --border: #e0e0e0;\n  --border-light: #d0d0d0;\n  --border-hover: #aaaaaa;\n  --border-strong: #cccccc;\n\n  --text-primary: #1a1a1a;\n  --text-secondary: #666666;\n  --text-muted: #999999;\n  --text-dim: #cccccc;\n  --text-inverse: #ffffff;\n  --text-danger: #cc0000;\n  --text-on-white: #000000;\n  --text-shiny-base: #000000;\n  --text-shiny-shine: #1a1a1a;\n\n  --shadow-card: 0 2px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\n  --shadow-hover: 0 0 16px rgba(0,0,0,0.06);\n  --shadow-menu: 0 8px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.12);\n\n  --scrollbar-track: #f0f0f0;\n  --scrollbar-thumb: #cccccc;\n  --scrollbar-thumb-hover: #aaaaaa;\n\n  --divider: #e0e0e0;\n\n  --progress-track: #e0e0e0;\n  --progress-fill: #1a1a1a;\n\n  --calendar-picker-filter: none;\n}\n\n.dark {\n  --bg-app: #000000;\n  --bg-card: #0a0a0a;\n  --bg-card-hover: #0d0d0d;\n  --bg-float: #080808;\n  --bg-float-hover: #0a0a0a;\n  --bg-input: #0a0a0a;\n  --bg-hover: #141414;\n  --bg-badge: #111111;\n  --bg-overlay: rgba(0,0,0,0.6);\n  --bg-toggle: #222222;\n  --bg-modal: #0a0a0a;\n  --bg-update: #0a0a0a;\n  --bg-menu: #0a0a0a;\n  --bg-menu-hover: #161616;\n  --bg-delete-hover: #1a0a0a;\n  --bg-dropdown: #0a0a0a;\n  --bg-scheduled: #0a0a0a;\n  --bg-tag: #111111;\n\n  --border: #1a1a1a;\n  --border-light: #222222;\n  --border-hover: #2e2e2e;\n  --border-strong: #2e2e2e;\n\n  --text-primary: #ededed;\n  --text-secondary: #888888;\n  --text-muted: #444444;\n  --text-dim: #2a2a2a;\n  --text-inverse: #000000;\n  --text-danger: #ff5555;\n  --text-on-white: #ffffff;\n  --text-shiny-base: #888888;\n  --text-shiny-shine: #ededed;\n\n  --shadow-card: 0 4px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.4);\n  --shadow-hover: 0 0 20px rgba(255,255,255,0.04);\n  --shadow-menu: 0 8px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);\n\n  --scrollbar-track: #000000;\n  --scrollbar-thumb: #1a1a1a;\n  --scrollbar-thumb-hover: #2a2a2a;\n\n  --divider: #1a1a1a;\n\n  --progress-track: #1a1a1a;\n  --progress-fill: #ffffff;\n\n  --calendar-picker-filter: invert(0.7);\n}\n\n* {\n  margin: 0;\n  padding: 0;\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n}\n\nhtml, body, #root {\n  background: var(--bg-app);\n  color: var(--text-primary);\n  font-family: 'Geist Mono', monospace;\n  width: 100%;\n  height: 100%;\n  -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;\n  -moz-osx-font-smoothing: grayscale;\n}\n\n/* ─── Scrollbar ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */\n\n::-webkit-scrollbar {\n  width: 3px;\n}\n\n::-webkit-scrollbar-track {\n  background: var(--scrollbar-track);\n}\n\n::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb {\n  background: var(--scrollbar-thumb);\n  border-radius: 3px;\n}\n\n::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:hover {\n  background: var(--scrollbar-thumb-hover);\n}\n\n/* ─── Date Input ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */\n\ninput[type=\"date\"]::-webkit-calendar-picker-indicator {\n  filter: var(--calendar-picker-filter);\n  cursor: pointer;\n}\n\n/* ─── Card Styles (.v-card) ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */\n\n.v-card {\n  background: var(--bg-card);\n  border: 1px solid var(--border);\n  border-radius: 10px;\n  padding: 12px 12px 12px 14px;\n  transition: all 0.15s ease;\n  cursor: default;\n}\n\n.v-card:hover {\n  border-color: var(--border-hover);\n  background: var(--bg-card-hover);\n}\n\n.v-card.completed {\n  opacity: 0.35;\n}\n\n.v-card.completed .task-title {\n  text-decoration: line-through;\n}\n\n/* ─── Floating Card Styles (.v-float) ──────────────────────────────────── */\n\n.v-float {\n  background: var(--bg-float);\n  border: 1px solid var(--border);\n  border-radius: 20px;\n  padding: 14px 16px;\n  transition: border-","createdAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.155Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mq6vxsy3_a689d81b01bf","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"File: src/index.css\n\n@import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist","type":"fact","updatedAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.155Z","version":1},"mem_mq6vxszu_21c8ae8d4194":{"concepts":[],"content":"File: postcss.config.js\n\nexport default {\n  plugins: {\n    tailwindcss: {},\n    autoprefixer: {},\n  },\n};","createdAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.207Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mq6vxszu_21c8ae8d4194","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"File: postcss.config.js\n\nexport default {\n  plugins: {\n    tailwindcss: {},\n    ","type":"fact","updatedAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.207Z","version":1},"mem_mq6vxt0y_ac1985d992e7":{"concepts":[],"content":"File: tailwind.config.ts\n\nimport type { Config } from \"tailwindcss\";\n\nconst config: Config = {\n  darkMode: [\"class\"],\n  content: [\n    \"./index.html\",\n    \"./src/**/*.{js,ts,jsx,tsx}\",\n  ],\n  theme: {\n    extend: {\n      colors: {\n        border: \"#1a1a1a\",\n        input: \"#1a1a1a\",\n        ring: \"#333\",\n        background: \"#000\",\n        foreground: \"#ededed\",\n        primary: {\n          DEFAULT: \"#fff\",\n          foreground: \"#000\",\n        },\n        secondary: {\n          DEFAULT: \"#0a0a0a\",\n          foreground: \"#888\",\n        },\n        destructive: {\n          DEFAULT: \"#444\",\n          foreground: \"#ededed\",\n        },\n        muted: {\n          DEFAULT: \"#0d0d0d\",\n          foreground: \"#444\",\n        },\n        accent: {\n          DEFAULT: \"#111\",\n          foreground: \"#ededed\",\n        },\n        popover: {\n          DEFAULT: \"#0a0a0a\",\n          foreground: \"#ededed\",\n        },\n        card: {\n          DEFAULT: \"#0a0a0a\",\n          foreground: \"#ededed\",\n        },\n      },\n      fontFamily: {\n        mono: [\"'Geist Mono'\", \"monospace\"],\n      },\n      borderRadius: {\n        lg: \"8px\",\n        md: \"6px\",\n        sm: \"4px\",\n      },\n    },\n  },\n  plugins: [],\n};\n\nexport default config;","createdAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.248Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mq6vxt0y_ac1985d992e7","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"File: tailwind.config.ts\n\nimport type { Config } from \"tailwindcss\";\n\nconst conf","type":"fact","updatedAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.248Z","version":1},"mem_mq6vxt23_b98afb5a4328":{"concepts":[],"content":"File: tsconfig.json\n\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2020\",\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": true,\n    \"lib\": [\"ES2020\", \"DOM\", \"DOM.Iterable\"],\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"resolveJsonModule\": true,\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"strict\": true,\n    \"noUnusedLocals\": false,\n    \"noUnusedParameters\": false,\n    \"noFallthroughCasesInSwitch\": true,\n    \"baseUrl\": \".\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\"./src/*\"]\n    }\n  },\n  \"include\": [\"src\"],\n  \"references\": [{ \"path\": \"./tsconfig.node.json\" }]\n}","createdAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.296Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mq6vxt23_b98afb5a4328","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"File: tsconfig.json\n\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2020\",\n    \"useDe","type":"fact","updatedAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.296Z","version":1},"mem_mq6vxt2s_f9995aae4e66":{"concepts":[],"content":"File: vite.config.ts\n\nimport { defineConfig } from \"vite\";\nimport react from \"@vitejs/plugin-react\";\nimport path from \"path\";\n\nconst host = process.env.TAURI_DEV_HOST;\n\nexport default defineConfig(async () => ({\n  plugins: [react()],\n  build: {\n    rollupOptions: {\n      input: {\n        main: \"index.html\",\n        taskCard: \"task-card.html\",\n        quickAdd: \"quick-add.html\",\n        dailyDigest: \"daily-digest.html\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  resolve: {\n    alias: {\n      \"@\": path.resolve(__dirname, \"./src\"),\n    },\n  },\n  clearScreen: false,\n  server: {\n    port: 1420,\n    strictPort: true,\n    host: host || false,\n    hmr: host\n      ? {\n          protocol: \"ws\",\n          host,\n          port: 1421,\n        }\n      : undefined,\n    watch: {\n      ignored: [\"**/src-tauri/**\"],\n    },\n  },\n}));","createdAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.322Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mq6vxt2s_f9995aae4e66","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"File: vite.config.ts\n\nimport { defineConfig } from \"vite\";\nimport react from \"@v","type":"fact","updatedAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.322Z","version":1},"mem_mq6vxt3k_8132578372fa":{"concepts":[],"content":"File: .github/workflows/release.yml\n\nname: Release\non:\n  push:\n    tags:\n      - 'v*'\n\njobs:\n  release:\n    strategy:\n      matrix:\n        os: [windows-latest, macos-latest, ubuntu-latest]\n    runs-on: ${{ matrix.os }}\n    permissions:\n      contents: write\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n\n      - name: Setup Node\n        uses: actions/setup-node@v4\n        with:\n          node-version: 20\n\n      - name: Setup Rust\n        uses: dtolnay/rust-toolchain@stable\n\n      - name: Install Linux dependencies\n        if: matrix.os == 'ubuntu-latest'\n        run: |\n          sudo apt-get update\n          sudo apt-get install -y \\\n            libwebkit2gtk-4.1-dev \\\n            libayatana-appindicator3-dev \\\n            librsvg2-dev \\\n            libgtk-3-dev \\\n            libsoup-3.0-dev \\\n            libjavascriptcoregtk-4.1-dev \\\n            libfuse2\n\n      - name: Install dependencies\n        run: npm install\n\n      - name: Build and publish\n        uses: tauri-apps/tauri-action@v0\n        env:\n          GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\n          TAURI_PRIVATE_KEY: ${{ secrets.TAURI_PRIVATE_KEY }}\n          TAURI_KEY_PASSWORD: ${{ secrets.TAURI_KEY_PASSWORD }}\n          TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY: ${{ secrets.TAURI_PRIVATE_KEY }}\n          TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY_PASSWORD: ${{ secrets.TAURI_KEY_PASSWORD }}\n        with:\n          tagName: ${{ github.ref_name }}\n          releaseName: PinedIn ${{ github.ref_name }}\n          releaseBody: \"See changelog for details.\"\n          releaseDraft: false\n          prerelease: false\n\n      - name: Upload to public release repo\n        env:\n          GH_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.PINEDIN_RELEASES_TOKEN }}\n        shell: bash\n        run: |\n          BUNDLE_DIR=\"src-tauri/target/release/bundle\"\n          [ ! -d \"$BUNDLE_DIR\" ] && echo \"No bundle dir\" && exit 0\n\n          RELEASE_TAG=\"${{ github.ref_name }}\"\n          PUBLIC_REPO=\"Zarl-prog/PinedIn-Releases\"\n\n          # Create the public release if it doesn't exist yet\n          gh release view \"$RELEASE_TAG\" --repo \"$PUBLIC_REPO\" &>/dev/null || \\\n            gh release create \"$RELEASE_TAG\" \\\n              --repo \"$PUBLIC_REPO\" \\\n              --title \"PinedIn $RELEASE_TAG\" \\\n              --notes \"See the main repo for changelog.\"\n\n          # Upload installer files (.exe, .dmg, .AppImage, .deb, .rpm)\n          find \"$BUNDLE_DIR\" -type f \\( -name \"*.exe\" -o -name \"*.dmg\" -o -name \"*.AppImage\" -o -name \"*.deb\" -o -name \"*.rpm\" \\) \\\n            -exec gh release upload \"$RELEASE_TAG\" {} --repo \"$PUBLIC_REPO\" --clobber \\;\n\n          # Upload updater archives — v1Compatible generates .tar.gz (macOS/Linux)\n          # and .zip (Windows) in bundle/updater/ or alongside bundles\n          UPDATER_DIR=\"$BUNDLE_DIR/updater\"\n          if [ -d \"$UPDATER_DIR\" ]; then\n            find \"$UPDATER_DIR\" -type f \\( -name \"*.tar.gz\" -o -name \"*.zip\" \\) \\\n              -exec gh release upload \"$RELEASE_TAG\" {} --repo \"$PUBLIC_REPO\" --clobber \\;\n            # Upload .sig signature files alongside the archives\n            find \"$UPDATER_DIR\" -type f -name \"*.sig\" \\\n              -exec gh release upload \"$RELEASE_TAG\" {} --repo \"$PUBLIC_REPO\" --clobber \\;\n          fi\n\n          # Also look for .sig files alongside installers (for non-v1Compatible)\n          find \"$BUNDLE_DIR\" -type f -name \"*.sig\" \\\n            -exec gh release upload \"$RELEASE_TAG\" {} --repo \"$PUBLIC_REPO\" --clobber \\;\n\n          # Generate latest.json from the updater archives that were uploaded\n          echo \"Generating latest.json from updater artifacts...\"\n          PLATFORMS=\"\"\n          for f in $(find \"$UPDATER_DIR\" -type f \\( -name \"*.tar.gz\" -o -name \"*.zip\" \\) 2>/dev/null); do\n            BASENAME=$(basename \"$f\")\n            # Extract platform from updater archive filename (Tauri v2 v1Compatible naming)\n            case \"$BASENAME\" in\n              *x64-setup.nsis.zip*)  PLAT=\"windows-x86_64\" ;;\n              *x64-setup.mui.zip*)   PLAT=\"windows-x86_64\" ;;\n              *x86_64-setup.nsis.zip*) PLAT=\"windows-x","createdAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.351Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mq6vxt3k_8132578372fa","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"File: .github/workflows/release.yml\n\nname: Release\non:\n  push:\n    tags:\n      -","type":"fact","updatedAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.351Z","version":1},"mem_mq6vxt4k_e2f2594898d7":{"concepts":[],"content":"Project source structure (src/):\nApp.tsx\ncomponents/AddTaskModal.tsx\ncomponents/DailyDigest.tsx\ncomponents/PreScheduleModal.tsx\ncomponents/QuickAdd.tsx\ncomponents/SettingsPanel.tsx\ncomponents/TaskCard.tsx\ncomponents/TaskList.tsx\ncomponents/ui/ShinyText.css\ncomponents/ui/ShinyText.tsx\ncomponents/UpdateBanner.tsx\ncomponents/UrgencyBadge.tsx\ncomponents/WorkspaceDetailView.tsx\ncomponents/WorkspacesView.tsx\ndaily-digest-main.tsx\nhooks/useReminders.ts\nhooks/useSettings.ts\nindex.css\nlib/tauriCommands.ts\nlib/updater.ts\nlib/utils.ts\nmain.tsx\nquick-add-main.tsx\nstore/reminderStore.ts\ntask-card-main.tsx\ntask-card.css","createdAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.388Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mq6vxt4k_e2f2594898d7","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"Project source structure (src/):\nApp.tsx\ncomponents/AddTaskModal.tsx\ncomponents/","type":"fact","updatedAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.388Z","version":1},"mem_mq6vxt57_1cbefbefc78d":{"concepts":[],"content":"Rust source structure (src-tauri/src/):\nsrc-tauri/src/commands.rs\nsrc-tauri/src/db.rs\nsrc-tauri/src/lib.rs\nsrc-tauri/src/main.rs\nsrc-tauri/src/notifications.rs\nsrc-tauri/src/scheduler.rs\nsrc-tauri/src/tray.rs\nsrc-tauri/src/window.rs","createdAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.411Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mq6vxt57_1cbefbefc78d","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"Rust source structure (src-tauri/src/):\nsrc-tauri/src/commands.rs\nsrc-tauri/src/","type":"fact","updatedAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.411Z","version":1},"mem_mq6vxt5w_4f6010746868":{"concepts":[],"content":"UI Framework: React 18 + TypeScript with Vite bundler","createdAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.434Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mq6vxt5w_4f6010746868","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"UI Framework: React 18 + TypeScript with Vite bundler","type":"fact","updatedAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.434Z","version":1},"mem_mq6vxt6h_01a433b2c30f":{"concepts":[],"content":"Desktop Framework: Tauri v2 (Rust backend, webview-based frontend)","createdAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.459Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mq6vxt6h_01a433b2c30f","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"Desktop Framework: Tauri v2 (Rust backend, webview-based frontend)","type":"fact","updatedAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.459Z","version":1},"mem_mq6vxt70_507218932790":{"concepts":[],"content":"Styling: Tailwind CSS with class-variance-authority for component variants","createdAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.478Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mq6vxt70_507218932790","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"Styling: Tailwind CSS with class-variance-authority for component variants","type":"fact","updatedAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.478Z","version":1},"mem_mq6vxt7h_af509b905c97":{"concepts":[],"content":"Animations: framer-motion for card animations, shakes, transitions","createdAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.496Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mq6vxt7h_af509b905c97","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"Animations: framer-motion for card animations, shakes, transitions","type":"fact","updatedAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.496Z","version":1},"mem_mq6vxt82_85523f1ca211":{"concepts":[],"content":"State Management: Zustand stores for tasks, reminders, workspaces","createdAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.512Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mq6vxt82_85523f1ca211","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"State Management: Zustand stores for tasks, reminders, workspaces","type":"fact","updatedAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.512Z","version":1},"mem_mq6vxt8n_bd0d6b65e93b":{"concepts":[],"content":"Window Management: Tauri window API — each task card is a separate webview window with custom decorations (no native titlebar), draggable via startDragging()","createdAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.532Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mq6vxt8n_bd0d6b65e93b","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"Window Management: Tauri window API — each task card is a separate webview windo","type":"fact","updatedAt":"2026-06-09T16:59:53.532Z","version":1},"mem_mq6vxt9